t_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.7.2 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 64 bits\n\n### Issue description\n\nBy default, ConfirmationDialog buttons are annoyingly narrow:\n\n<img width=\"417\" height=\"174\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/06ff123b-9dec-4825-8b9a-b3ce45284b49\" />\n\nSo I usually widen them by setting their `custom_minimum_size`. I do it in my C++ module and that usually works: https://github.com/Zylann/godot_voxel/blob/14f4996b0d736d9cbdeb0748ec69e7dcc80e177e/editor/about_window.cpp#L359\n\nHowever when I'm doing it in a game with GDScript, no matter how I try, it never works. The property gets set, but the button doesn't get larger, and checking/printing the property later shows it constantly reverts to (0,0).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name MyDialog\nextends ConfirmationDialog\n\n\nfunc _init() -> void:\n\tprint(\"Init Before: \", get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size)\n\tget_ok_button().custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 0)\n\tprint(\"Init After: \", get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size)\n\n\n#func _ready() -> void:\n\t#print(\"Ready: \", get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size)\n\t#get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 0)\n\t#print(\"Ready: \", get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size)\n\n\n#func _process(delta: float) -> void:\n\t#print(\"Before: \", get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size)\n\t#get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size = Vector2(200, 0)\n\t#print(\"After: \", get_ok_button().custom_minimum_size)\n```\nWhen trying the `_process` approach, it shows the property gets reverted to (0,0), every frame, as long as the dialog is visible.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[DialogButtonsMinSize.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32077887/DialogButtonsMinSize.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avata